\ A recursive word that reaches its recursion through a tail-position `call`.
\
\ `when` is the last word of `r`, so it is a free tail call, and its `if` is the last word of
\ `when`. Each level is one `if` arm, one `call` body, both entered by a native in tail position,
\ and one non-tail call to `r`.

r: stack-recursive ( n -- n ) [ dup 0 > [ [ 1 - r 1 + ] call ] when ] ;

12 r drop
